{
 "description": "Single-screen mode (emulator only). images: pictures the layouts add (png: a file of interface/single_screen/layout/images/; texture: its name in the game's ARCs; the other keys are the numbers of tools/inspect/world_map_paper.py, which makes the world map's paper from a photograph); a layout's layers puts one right after its sprite `after`, fitted over the groups `over` grown by `margin` (like fit). The layouts that were on the 320x240 touch screen are loaded on the 400x240 top screen (top_screen: by the executable's bytes), so each one is scaled by `factor` (0-1) and pushed against the screen edge or corner `anchor` (left, right, top, bottom, top_left, top_right, bottom_left, bottom_right or center); a layout without both is not moved. `priority` is added to the draw priority of its groups (higher is in front), `group_priority` replaces it for single groups; `backdrop` is a group of the layout stretched over the whole top screen instead; `hide` lists groups made clear; `fixed` lists root groups left exactly as the file has them (not scaled, moved, measured nor given the layout's priority: the DLC scene's wooden frame, which the placed panels stand in front of); `push` lists groups moved on their own to the anchor's edge after the placing; `fill` adds a copy of the sprite `template` as the first child of `group`, over the whole top screen or over the groups of `over` grown by `margin`, tinted by `color` (RGBA). prompt_stay_bottom: groups of the yes / no box (ui006) left on the touch screen while a prompt is open. `character_shift` (0-110, world units, about 1 px each): the boot's save list (ui803) hides the Felyne of the choose-character scene, so its hunter (x 40) and Felyne (x -60) models move right by this much, each turned to keep facing the camera; the hunter clips at about x 150, so 110 is the top. creation_camera: the new game's character creation (ui800, ui415, ui802 on the top screen, the menus at the right): per camera mode (0 hunter, 1 face/eyes/features, 2 hair, 3 Felyne, 4 Felyne eyes/ears, 5 both models at the final confirm) model_left = pixels the 3D model moves left of the screen's centre and distance = factor of the camera's distance. creation_prompt: the creation's help text and OK / Back buttons (ui006) go to the top screen while one of the root groups in `groups` (at most 8) is shown, each ui006 group moved by `shift` (name -> [dx, dy] pixels, right and down, from the layout's own place); the yes / no boxes keep the layout's place; while a group of `unless` is shown (ui470_base, the Palico menus' board, whose clothes chooser shows the creation's groups) the creation's menu mode is off. creation_boards: the creation's name boards (ui802_l_player the hunter's, ui802_l_otomo the Felyne's) are shown only on the pages (kinds) in `kinds` (0 the hunter's main menu, 15 the Felyne's; the sub-menus are 1-14 and 16-24, the name keyboards 1 and 16), hidden on the rest; the game shows them on every page; a layout's `nudge` puts each board in the free cell of its main menu's button grid. In a layout, `move` \"none\" only scales (the `offset` places it) and `wrap` lists panes the game's code positions in the file's own units (cursors), kept in a null that takes the factor. keyboard (the name keyboard, driven with the pad by a virtual finger): `delete` and `ok` are the names of the keyboard's controls that B and START touch (G_key_Bsp the delete key, G_btn_02 the right button), `start` the touch point (x, y of the 320 x 240 touch screen) the finger starts nearest to; the D-pad's choice of the next control: `slack` pixels a control may overlap the hover's edge and still lie in that direction, `across_weight` and `centre_weight` the whole numbers that multiply the gap across (between the two controls' extents) and the distance between their middles across, added to the gap ahead; `tab_hover` the colour (RRGGBB) a hovered mode tab is tinted with (the tabs have no pressed look the finger can use), `skip` the names of controls the finger never rests on (the text area: it shows the name, it is no target); `backdrop_width` the pixels the keyboard's own background is widened to (the top screen's 400, so it covers the strips of scene at the sides; 320 leaves it as it was). help_top (the touch menus' description panel, ui006_help00 and the groups of `also`, on the top screen): in a game mode of `quest_scenes` (the game control's byte +0x2B: 1 a quest, 5 its results) only the places with `quest` true may be taken (the quest rewards place, under the rewards screen's panels); while no yes / no prompt is open and no creation menu is shown, no group of `stay_bottom` shown keeps the panel on the touch screen; else the first of `places` whose `when` is empty or has a group shown, and whose `unless` has no group shown and whose `unless_flags` (a variable of the mod: screens_open, the layered selector's frame is open) has none set, puts the panel on the top screen at its `shift` (pixels right and down from the layout's own place, the yes / no box's), and the other ui006 groups in that place's `groups` (name -> [dx, dy], optional; the Canteen's three pay buttons, in a row under the effects panel, left to right in the order of the pay choice's cursor; the Wyporio's two confirm buttons, stacked under its panel in the bottom left corner; the hunter search's OK and Cancel buttons, stacked right of the panel under the world map's board, the row centred; the Palico menus' key hint) go to the top screen with it, each at its own shift, and back down when the place is left; no place fits: it stays on the touch screen. The groups are root groups of the touch menus' layouts; each place's `unless` is the groups whose boxes reach that place's strip (x 186-378 for the right strip, x 4-196 for the left one, both y 196-234); the 'trade list' place (Wyporium's) sits in the left column between its panels, where the two-column list leaves no free strip; the Smithy's craft list has no free place and keeps it on the touch screen. arena_choice (the Arena's select scene, whose layouts ui497 and ui498 the game GUI engine places): the places, pixels right and down from the layout file's, that the scene's code gives the info panels in its other modes, weapon_detail the equipment panel's, skills_overview the skills', status_overview the status'; up the button, 1-4 from the left, the pad's up goes to from each of the five weapon sets; the frame around the choice's buttons follows their nudges (game_gui/fixes.json), whole units of the file; the description panel stays on the touch screen in every mode of the scene: `ui497_ui497` is in help_top's stay_bottom. The 'palico clothes', 'palico main info' and 'palico' places put the panel under the Palico menus' panels (the clothes chooser's Back button stays on the touch screen; the key hint 'Y Palico Info' goes above the panel with Main Palico Info and beside it elsewhere). frames (the Palico menus): every root group of `sets` (name -> groups; at most 16 sets and 160 groups) is wrapped in a null, <group>_frame, that the executable moves and scales while the groups shown fit a scene: the first of `scenes` whose `all` groups are all shown, whose `any` has one shown (or is empty) and whose `none` has none shown (at most 16 scenes, 32 distinct groups in their lists) puts each set of its `frames` at `scale` (0.3-1) and `at` (pixels), a point (x, y) of the top screen going to (scale x + at x, scale y + at y); a set the scene leaves out, and every set when no scene fits, keeps the layout's own place. `only_in`: a layout whose groups are framed only in the ARCs named (the clothes chooser ui415 in the Palico rooms, not on the title's creation). `prompt_off`: sets of `sets` left at their own place (no frame) while a yes / no prompt is open (the description panel: its question stays with its buttons).",
